Doja Cat Appears Not to Have Any Idea Who Ella Langley Is: &#8216;I Don&#8217;t&nbsp;Know&#8217;

Will Ella Langley&#8217;s &#8216;Choosin&#8217; Texas&#8217; Pass Mariah Carey&#8217;s &#8216;Christmas&#8217; for the All-Time Hot 100 Record for Weeks at No. 1 — And Then Just Keep&nbsp;Going?

In a Thursday (Aug. 27) post on Instagram featuring photos and videos from her recent travels and performances, Langley appeared to lightheartedly poke fun at the rapper&#8217;s comments about her by writing in the caption, &#8220;Ella Langley? What is that?&#8221;

The post itself wasn&#8217;t related to Doja, with some slides showing Langley on an airplane and others capturing the Alabama native getting her makeup done, holding a butterfly or cuddling with an adorable dog.

It comes a few days after the &#8220;Say So&#8221; artist guested on Sundae Conversation and, with her signature candor, responded to a question about whether she was a fan of Langley&#8217;s with, “I don’t know what that is. Ella Langley?&#8221;

After her initial comments were met with disbelief from fans, Doja said she listened to Langley&#8217;s record-tying 19-week Billboard Hot 100 -topping smash &#8220;Choosin&#8217; Texas&#8221; for the first time on a livestream. The hip-hop hitmaker acknowledged that Langley has &#8220;a very pretty voice,&#8217; but ultimately said that she just doesn&#8217;t &#8220;give a f–k about country music.&#8221;

&#8220;I don’t understand what’s so hard to believe about that,&#8221; Doja continued on the stream. &#8220;I never cared. I like that one Keith Urban song from 2004. I wouldn’t say that I like [Langley&#8217;s] music; she’s probably a fine lady. I don’t care for that type of s–t at all. It doesn’t inspire me, it doesn’t make me feel good.&#8221;

“This is not my vibe, but she has a very pretty voice,” she added. “If this is No. 1 on the charts, I’m sure it’s on the radio. I could see them playing this s–t on the radio. I don’t like it, but that’s fine. It’s very earwormy it sounds like, it’s like catchy melody. I get it, and she’s pretty.”

But while Doja isn&#8217;t a fan of &#8220;Choosin&#8217; Texas,&#8221; it&#8217;s clear that countless other people are. The song recently tied Lil Nas X and Billy Ray Cyrus&#8217; &#8220;Old Town Road&#8221; for second-most weeks at No. 1 on the Hot 100. If it remains at the top for another seven days, it&#8217;ll tie Mariah Carey&#8217;s &#8220;All I Want for Christmas Is You&#8221; for the longest reign at the chart&#8217;s summit.
